{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'git diff ca66b77..8432edb -- pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_budget_test.go .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json POSE.md locales/pt-BR/POSE.md'","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json b/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\nindex 3d3fa181..babee280 100644\n--- a/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n+++ b/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n@@ -2419,10 +2419,17 @@\n           \"severity\": \"required\",\n           \"evidenceClass\": \"integration\"\n         },\n+        {\n+          \"name\": \"git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree-integration\",\n+          \"program\": \"go\",\n+          \"args\": [\"test\", \"./internal/pose\", \"-run\", \"TestGitSnapshotBudget|TestReviewWorktreeCleanup|TestGitTreeListingIsBounded|TestGovernedTreeListingIsBounded\", \"-count=1\"],\n+          \"severity\": \"required\",\n+          \"evidenceClass\": \"integration\"\n+        },\n         {\n           \"name\": \"doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\",\n           \"program\": \"go\",\n-          \"args\": [\"test\", \"./internal/cli\", \"-run\", \"TestDoctorRecommendsTheCommitGraph|TestDoctorCommitGraphReportsAnUnreadableHistory|TestDoctorCommitGraphTellsUnbornFromBroken|TestDoctorCommitGraphProbesALiteralPath|TestDoctorCommitGraphNamesDisabledReads\", \"-count=1\"],\n+          \"args\": [\"test\", \"./internal/cli\", \"-run\", \"TestDoctorRecommendsTheCommitGraph|TestDoctorCommitGraph\", \"-count=1\"],\n           \"severity\": \"required\",\n           \"evidenceClass\": \"integration\"\n         },\ndiff --git a/POSE.md b/POSE.md\nindex 62a2b263..f1a52434 100644\n--- a/POSE.md\n+++ b/POSE.md\n@@ -1020,7 +1020,7 @@ Use a positive timeout from 1ms to 24h (omitted: 60m). Omit `max_runs_per_bundle\n \n Bound setup to two minutes and 64KiB of discarded diagnostic capture; disable ambient checkout hooks. Bound concurrent stdout/stderr together during capture and read `{output}` through a root descriptor opened before spawn, refusing links, special files, identity changes and oversized files. Notes must be regular non-symlink UTF-8 files up to 16KiB. Do not interpolate brief/notes into shell code. Truncated, unsafe or unredactable channels make the execution failed/incomplete; withhold their bytes because a cutoff can split a credential. No such draft governs review authority. Caller cancellation and CLI interrupt/termination signals stop the covered process set; pipe wait is bounded.\n \n-Inspect `safety` on the immutable run, CLI dispatch/verify/resume and the existing MCP review-bundle projection. It reports profile/platform, available/unavailable capabilities, limits, capture completeness, execution cause, runtime resource identifier and the B12 cleanup OperationResult. Cleanup verifies operation ownership and removes only the captured workspace and its exact Git registration through confined descriptors, never a global Git prune. Inventory caps are 100000 workspace entries/256MiB, 1024 registration entries/256MiB and 4096 runtime entries/128MiB, depth 128. OS filesystem calls remain subject to I/O latency; no hard syscall deadline is claimed. Failure retains uncertain resources and is separate from the domain draft. It returns an operational error, blocks authority/continuation and remains an error on idempotent replay, without another spawn. Inspect the recorded runtime identifier and registration rather than rerunning the adapter to compensate.\n+Inspect `safety` on the immutable run, CLI dispatch/verify/resume and the existing MCP review-bundle projection. It reports profile/platform, available/unavailable capabilities, limits, capture completeness, execution cause, runtime resource identifier and the B12 cleanup OperationResult. Cleanup verifies operation ownership and removes only the captured workspace and its exact Git registration through confined descriptors, never a global Git prune. Inventory caps are 100000 workspace entries and the checked-out commit's tree bytes plus 256MiB (at least 256MiB, at most 4GiB), 1024 registration entries/256MiB and 4096 runtime entries/128MiB, depth 128. OS filesystem calls remain subject to I/O latency; no hard syscall deadline is claimed. Failure retains uncertain resources and is separate from the domain draft. It returns an operational error, blocks authority/continuation and remains an error on idempotent replay, without another spawn. Inspect the recorded runtime identifier and registration rather than rerunning the adapter to compensate.\n \n Retain evidence without automatic expiry (`retention_ttl_seconds: 0`); newly written run/transcript files use mode 0600 and private sessions retain their existing 0700/0600 policy. Export retained redacted run/transcript, witness, attempt/continuation receipts and optional proof together, preserving inventory and digests; exclude private sessions and issuer keys. Raw-byte digests precede redaction; retained-byte digests, canonical run identity, witness and native signature follow. No retention operation removes rejection history or restores quota. Legacy records remain readable with no fabricated safety observations. No instance policy, sandbox backend or real vendor is activated by these examples.\n \ndiff --git a/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md b/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\nindex 795ceadc..aa82662b 100644\n--- a/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n+++ b/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n@@ -1017,7 +1017,7 @@ Use timeout de 1ms a 24h, default 60m. Omita `max_runs_per_bundle` para default\n \n Limite setup a dois minutos/64KiB de diagnóstico descartado e desative hooks de checkout não selados. Capture stdout/stderr juntos com orçamento finito; leia `{output}` por descritor da raiz aberto antes do spawn. Recuse symlinks, arquivos especiais, identidade alterada e excesso de bytes. Notas exigem arquivo regular sem symlink, UTF-8 até 16KiB. Não interpole brief/notas em shell. Captura truncada/insegura ou impossível de redigir vira failed/incomplete e retém zero bytes dos canais: um corte pode dividir credencial. O draft não governa autoridade. Cancelamento do caller e sinais de interrupção/término CLI encerram o conjunto coberto; espera de pipes é limitada.\n \n-Consulte `safety` no run imutável, CLI dispatch/verify/resume e projeção MCP review-bundle existente: profile/platform, capacidades disponíveis/indisponíveis, limites, completude, causa, identificador de runtime e OperationResult B12 de cleanup. Cleanup valida ownership e remove workspace/registro Git exato pelos descritores confinados; nunca faça prune global. Inventários: workspace 100000 entradas/256MiB, registro 1024/256MiB, runtime 4096/128MiB, profundidade 128. Chamadas filesystem dependem de latência de I/O; nenhum deadline absoluto de syscall é alegado. Falha mantém recursos incertos, separada do draft de domínio, devolve erro operacional, bloqueia autoridade/continuação e permanece erro em replay idempotente sem novo spawn. Inspecione o identificador de runtime e seu registro em vez de reexecutar como compensação.\n+Consulte `safety` no run imutável, CLI dispatch/verify/resume e projeção MCP review-bundle existente: profile/platform, capacidades disponíveis/indisponíveis, limites, completude, causa, identificador de runtime e OperationResult B12 de cleanup. Cleanup valida ownership e remove workspace/registro Git exato pelos descritores confinados; nunca faça prune global. Inventários: workspace 100000 entradas e os bytes da árvore do commit em checkout mais 256MiB (no mínimo 256MiB, no máximo 4GiB), registro 1024/256MiB, runtime 4096/128MiB, profundidade 128. Chamadas filesystem dependem de latência de I/O; nenhum deadline absoluto de syscall é alegado. Falha mantém recursos incertos, separada do draft de domínio, devolve erro operacional, bloqueia autoridade/continuação e permanece erro em replay idempotente sem novo spawn. Inspecione o identificador de runtime e seu registro em vez de reexecutar como compensação.\n \n Retenha evidência sem expiração automática (`retention_ttl_seconds: 0`). Run/transcript novos usam 0600; sessões privadas mantêm 0700/0600. Exporte run/transcript redigidos, witness, recibos de tentativa/continuação e prova opcional juntos, conservando inventário/digests; exclua sessões privadas/chaves de issuer. Digests raw precedem redação; depois vêm digests retidos, identidade canônica, witness e assinatura nativa. Retenção não apaga rejeições nem restaura cota. Registros legados continuam legíveis sem observações inventadas de segurança. Exemplos não ativam policy, backend sandbox ou fornecedor real.\n \ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_budget_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_budget_test.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..2fb698be\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_budget_test.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,216 @@\n+package pose\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"bytes\"\n+\t\"os\"\n+\t\"path/filepath\"\n+\t\"strings\"\n+\t\"testing\"\n+\t\"time\"\n+)\n+\n+// snapshotBudgetRepo is a committed repository of four 4 KiB files, with the\n+// snapshot margin lowered to 1 KiB: its committed tree alone is past the\n+// margin, as pose-dist's 256.8 MiB tree is past the old 256 MiB bound.\n+func snapshotBudgetRepo(t *testing.T) (string, string) {\n+\tt.Helper()\n+\toriginal := gitSnapshotMarginBytes\n+\tt.Cleanup(func() { gitSnapshotMarginBytes = original })\n+\tgitSnapshotMarginBytes = 1 << 10\n+\troot := t.TempDir()\n+\tfederatedTestGit(t, root, \"init\", \"-q\")\n+\tfor _, kv := range [][]string{{\"user.name\", \"fixture\"}, {\"user.email\", \"fixture@example.invalid\"}, {\"commit.gpgsign\", \"false\"}} {\n+\t\tfederatedTestGit(t, root, \"config\", kv[0], kv[1])\n+\t}\n+\tfor i := 0; i < 4; i++ {\n+\t\tname := filepath.Join(root, \"data-\"+string(rune('a'+i))+\".txt\")\n+\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(name, bytes.Repeat([]byte{'x'}, 4<<10), 0o644); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tfederatedTestGit(t, root, \"add\", \"-A\")\n+\tfederatedTestGit(t, root, \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"data\")\n+\thead, err := gitCommand(\"-C\", root, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\").Output()\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\treturn root, strings.TrimSpace(string(head))\n+}\n+\n+// Spec pose-git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree, R1: a committed tree\n+// larger than the margin is compared and snapshotted whole.\n+func TestGitSnapshotBudgetCoversTheCommittedTree(t *testing.T) {\n+\troot, head := snapshotBudgetRepo(t)\n+\tchanged, err := gitMaterializedChanges(root, head)\n+\tif err != nil || len(changed) != 0 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a clean tree past the margin: changed=%v err=%v\", changed, err)\n+\t}\n+\tentries, err := dispatchDiskSnapshot(root)\n+\tif err != nil || len(entries) < 4 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a disk snapshot of a tree past the margin: %d entries, err=%v\", len(entries), err)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// R2: disk that grew past the committed tree by more than the margin still\n+// fails closed.\n+func TestGitSnapshotBudgetStillBoundsGrowth(t *testing.T) {\n+\troot, head := snapshotBudgetRepo(t)\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(root, \"data-a.txt\"), bytes.Repeat([]byte{'y'}, 64<<10), 0o644); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := gitMaterializedChanges(root, head); err == nil || !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"budget\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a tree that grew past its budget: %v, want a budget failure\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := dispatchDiskSnapshot(root); err == nil || !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"budget\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a disk that grew past its budget: %v, want a budget failure\", err)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// R3: the budget is never below the margin and never above the ceiling.\n+func TestGitSnapshotBudgetIsBounded(t *testing.T) {\n+\tif got := gitSnapshotBudget(0); got != gitSnapshotMarginBytes {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"an empty tree: %d, want the margin %d\", got, gitSnapshotMarginBytes)\n+\t}\n+\tif got := gitSnapshotBudget(1 << 40); got != gitSnapshotCeilingBytes {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a huge tree: %d, want the ceiling %d\", got, gitSnapshotCeilingBytes)\n+\t}\n+\tif got := gitSnapshotBudget(-5); got != gitSnapshotMarginBytes {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a negative size: %d\", got)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// cleanupBudgetFixture registers a detached review worktree of a commit\n+// whose tree is 4 KiB, with the snapshot margin lowered to 1 KiB, as\n+// dispatch does, and captures its cleanup ownership.\n+func cleanupBudgetFixture(t *testing.T, extra int) (Store, string, os.FileInfo, string, os.FileInfo, []byte, *reviewCleanupOwnership) {\n+\tt.Helper()\n+\toriginal := gitSnapshotMarginBytes\n+\tt.Cleanup(func() { gitSnapshotMarginBytes = original })\n+\tgitSnapshotMarginBytes = 1 << 10\n+\trepo := t.TempDir()\n+\tfederatedTestGit(t, repo, \"init\", \"-q\")\n+\tfor _, kv := range [][]string{{\"user.name\", \"fixture\"}, {\"user.email\", \"fixture@example.invalid\"}, {\"commit.gpgsign\", \"false\"}} {\n+\t\tfederatedTestGit(t, repo, \"config\", kv[0], kv[1])\n+\t}\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(repo, \"tracked\"), bytes.Repeat([]byte{'x'}, 4<<10), 0o600); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tfederatedTestGit(t, repo, \"add\", \"-A\")\n+\tfederatedTestGit(t, repo, \"commit\", \"-qm\", \"fixture\")\n+\ttmp := filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), \"operation\")\n+\tif err := os.Mkdir(tmp, 0o700); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\towned, err := os.Lstat(tmp)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\troot, err := os.OpenRoot(tmp)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tt.Cleanup(func() { root.Close() })\n+\tworktree := filepath.Join(tmp, \"worktree\")\n+\tfederatedTestGit(t, repo, \"worktree\", \"add\", \"-q\", \"--detach\", worktree, \"HEAD\")\n+\tif extra > 0 {\n+\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(worktree, \"grown\"), bytes.Repeat([]byte{'y'}, extra), 0o600); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tworktreeOwned, err := os.Lstat(worktree)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tmarker, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(worktree, \".git\"))\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tstore := Store{Root: repo}\n+\townership, err := store.captureReviewCleanupOwnership(root, worktree, marker)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\treturn store, tmp, owned, worktree, worktreeOwned, marker, ownership\n+}\n+\n+// R1: a review worktree whose checked-out tree is past the margin is\n+// removed whole by its cleanup.\n+func TestReviewWorktreeCleanupCoversTheCommittedTree(t *testing.T) {\n+\tstore, tmp, owned, worktree, worktreeOwned, marker, ownership := cleanupBudgetFixture(t, 0)\n+\tif err := store.cleanupReviewResources(tmp, owned, worktree, worktreeOwned, marker, ownership); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"cleanup of a worktree past the margin: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := os.Lstat(worktree); !os.IsNotExist(err) {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the worktree was not removed: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// R2: a worktree that grew past its committed tree by more than the margin\n+// keeps failing closed.\n+func TestReviewWorktreeCleanupStillBoundsGrowth(t *testing.T) {\n+\tstore, tmp, owned, worktree, worktreeOwned, marker, ownership := cleanupBudgetFixture(t, 64<<10)\n+\tif err := store.cleanupReviewResources(tmp, owned, worktree, worktreeOwned, marker, ownership); err == nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"cleanup of a worktree grown past its budget succeeded\")\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := os.Lstat(filepath.Join(worktree, \"grown\")); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a refused cleanup removed the worktree's contents: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// Review N2: a tree listing past its bound is not retained; the comparison\n+// fails, and the disk snapshot and the cleanup fall back to the margin alone,\n+// which a tree past the margin exceeds, so all three fail closed.\n+func TestGitTreeListingIsBounded(t *testing.T) {\n+\toriginal := gitTreeListingMaxBytes\n+\tt.Cleanup(func() { gitTreeListingMaxBytes = original })\n+\troot, head := snapshotBudgetRepo(t)\n+\tgitTreeListingMaxBytes = 64\n+\tif _, err := listCommittedTree(root, head); err == nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"a listing past its bound was returned\")\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := gitMaterializedChanges(root, head); err == nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"the comparison accepted a listing past its bound\")\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := dispatchDiskSnapshot(root); err == nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"the disk snapshot of a tree past the margin succeeded without its listing\")\n+\t}\n+\tstore, tmp, owned, worktree, worktreeOwned, marker, ownership := cleanupBudgetFixture(t, 0)\n+\tif ownership.inventoryBytes != gitSnapshotMarginBytes {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the cleanup budget was computed from a listing past its bound: %d\", ownership.inventoryBytes)\n+\t}\n+\tif err := store.cleanupReviewResources(tmp, owned, worktree, worktreeOwned, marker, ownership); err == nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"the cleanup of a worktree past the margin succeeded without its listing\")\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// Review N4: the governed comparison a closeout runs under its producer\n+// bounds the listing by the same bytes and deadline, and keeps working\n+// within them.\n+func TestGovernedTreeListingIsBounded(t *testing.T) {\n+\troot, head := snapshotBudgetRepo(t)\n+\tgoverned := func() error {\n+\t\t_, view := Store{Root: root}.beginGovernanceReadView()\n+\t\tif view == nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"no read view\")\n+\t\t}\n+\t\t_, err := gitMaterializedChangesForIn(view.filesFor(\"closeout-plan\"), root, head, nil, \"closeout-plan\")\n+\t\treturn err\n+\t}\n+\tif err := governed(); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the governed comparison within its bounds: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tmaxBytes, timeout := gitTreeListingMaxBytes, gitTreeListingTimeout\n+\tt.Cleanup(func() { gitTreeListingMaxBytes, gitTreeListingTimeout = maxBytes, timeout })\n+\tgitTreeListingMaxBytes = 64\n+\tif err := governed(); err == nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"the governed comparison accepted a listing past its byte bound\")\n+\t}\n+\tgitTreeListingMaxBytes = maxBytes\n+\tgitTreeListingTimeout = time.Nanosecond\n+\tif err := governed(); err == nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"the governed comparison accepted a listing past its deadline\")\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := listCommittedTree(root, head); err == nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"a listing past its deadline was returned\")\n+\t}\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go\nindex db9df7a2..82f8cbea 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go\n@@ -17,14 +17,73 @@ import (\n \t\"path/filepath\"\n \t\"runtime\"\n \t\"sort\"\n+\t\"strconv\"\n \t\"strings\"\n+\t\"time\"\n )\n \n+// The bytes a snapshot reads are bounded by the committed tree it compares\n+// against plus a margin, never less than the margin alone and never more than\n+// the ceiling: a fixed bound stopped every closeout once a repository's\n+// committed tree outgrew it (spec pose-git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree).\n+var (\n+\tgitSnapshotMarginBytes  int64 = 256 << 20\n+\tgitSnapshotCeilingBytes int64 = 4 << 30\n+)\n+\n+func gitSnapshotBudget(committedBytes int64) int64 {\n+\tif committedBytes < 0 {\n+\t\tcommittedBytes = 0\n+\t}\n+\tif committedBytes > gitSnapshotCeilingBytes-gitSnapshotMarginBytes {\n+\t\treturn gitSnapshotCeilingBytes\n+\t}\n+\treturn committedBytes + gitSnapshotMarginBytes\n+}\n+\n+// A committed tree listing is read through a bounded buffer under a\n+// deadline: 100,000 entries of ordinary paths fit well inside it, and a\n+// listing past it fails closed before it is retained (review N2).\n+var (\n+\tgitTreeListingMaxBytes int64 = 64 << 20\n+\tgitTreeListingTimeout        = 2 * time.Minute\n+)\n+\n+// listCommittedTree returns `ls-tree -r -l -z commit` of root, bounded.\n+func listCommittedTree(root, commit string) ([]byte, error) {\n+\tctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), gitTreeListingTimeout)\n+\tdefer cancel()\n+\treturn runGovernanceGitCommandContext(ctx, NativeFiles(), root, []string{\"ls-tree\", \"-r\", \"-l\", \"-z\", commit}, gitTreeListingMaxBytes)\n+}\n+\n+// gitCommittedTreeBytes sums the blob sizes of an `ls-tree -r -l -z` listing.\n+func gitCommittedTreeBytes(listing []byte) int64 {\n+\tvar total int64\n+\tfor _, record := range bytes.Split(listing, []byte{0}) {\n+\t\ti := bytes.IndexByte(record, '\\t')\n+\t\tif i < 0 {\n+\t\t\tcontinue\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tfields := strings.Fields(string(record[:i]))\n+\t\tif len(fields) == 4 {\n+\t\t\tif size, err := strconv.ParseInt(fields[3], 10, 64); err == nil && size > 0 {\n+\t\t\t\ttotal += size\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\treturn total\n+}\n+\n // Snapshot disk, including ignored files. Git status alone cannot witness\n // creation of an ignored output. WalkDir never follows a directory symlink.\n func dispatchDiskSnapshot(root string) (map[string]string, error) {\n \tentries := map[string]string{}\n \tvar total int64\n+\tcommitted := int64(0)\n+\tif listing, err := listCommittedTree(root, \"HEAD\"); err == nil {\n+\t\tcommitted = gitCommittedTreeBytes(listing)\n+\t}\n+\tbudget := gitSnapshotBudget(committed)\n \terr := filepath.WalkDir(root, func(path string, entry fs.DirEntry, err error) error {\n \t\tif err != nil {\n \t\t\treturn err\n@@ -63,7 +122,7 @@ func dispatchDiskSnapshot(root string) (map[string]string, error) {\n \t\t\tif err != nil {\n \t\t\t\treturn err\n \t\t\t}\n-\t\t\tn, readErr := io.Copy(hash, io.LimitReader(file, (256<<20)-total+1))\n+\t\t\tn, readErr := io.Copy(hash, io.LimitReader(file, budget-total+1))\n \t\t\tcloseErr := file.Close()\n \t\t\ttotal += n\n \t\t\tif readErr != nil {\n@@ -72,8 +131,8 @@ func dispatchDiskSnapshot(root string) (map[string]string, error) {\n \t\t\tif closeErr != nil {\n \t\t\t\treturn closeErr\n \t\t\t}\n-\t\t\tif total > 256<<20 {\n-\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"disk snapshot exceeds 256 MiB\")\n+\t\t\tif total > budget {\n+\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"disk snapshot exceeds its budget of %d bytes\", budget)\n \t\t\t}\n \t\tcase info.Mode()&os.ModeSymlink != 0:\n \t\t\ttarget, err := os.Readlink(path)\n@@ -176,10 +235,22 @@ func gitMaterializedChangesForIn(files Files, root, commit string, matters func(\n \tif producer != \"\" {\n \t\tproducer = governanceProducerFromFiles(files, producer)\n \t}\n-\trunGit := snapshotGit\n+\trunGit := func(root string, args ...string) ([]byte, error) {\n+\t\tif len(args) == 5 && args[0] == \"ls-tree\" {\n+\t\t\treturn listCommittedTree(root, args[4])\n+\t\t}\n+\t\treturn snapshotGit(root, args...)\n+\t}\n \tworktreeIdentity := dispatchWorktreeIdentity\n \tif producer != \"\" {\n \t\trunGit = func(root string, args ...string) ([]byte, error) {\n+\t\t\tif len(args) == 5 && args[0] == \"ls-tree\" {\n+\t\t\t\t// The governed listing keeps its read-view provenance under the\n+\t\t\t\t// listing's own bound and deadline (review N4).\n+\t\t\t\tctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), gitTreeListingTimeout)\n+\t\t\t\tdefer cancel()\n+\t\t\t\treturn CaptureGovernanceGitContextIn(files, ctx, root, producer, gitTreeListingMaxBytes, args...)\n+\t\t\t}\n \t\t\treturn captureGovernanceGit(files, root, producer, args...)\n \t\t}\n \t\tworktreeIdentity = func(root string) (string, error) {\n@@ -194,10 +265,11 @@ func gitMaterializedChangesForIn(files Files, root, commit string, matters func(\n \tif _, err := worktreeIdentity(root); err != nil {\n \t\treturn nil, err\n \t}\n-\tout, err := runGit(root, \"ls-tree\", \"-r\", \"-z\", commit)\n+\tout, err := runGit(root, \"ls-tree\", \"-r\", \"-l\", \"-z\", commit)\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn nil, err\n \t}\n+\tbudget := gitSnapshotBudget(gitCommittedTreeBytes(out))\n \tvar changed []string\n \tvar total int64\n \tcount := 0\n@@ -214,9 +286,10 @@ func gitMaterializedChangesForIn(files Files, root, commit string, matters func(\n \t\t\treturn nil, &GitSnapshotError{\"tree protocol\", fmt.Errorf(\"missing path\")}\n \t\t}\n \t\tfields := strings.Fields(string(record[:i]))\n-\t\tif len(fields) != 3 {\n+\t\tif len(fields) != 4 {\n \t\t\treturn nil, &GitSnapshotError{\"tree protocol\", fmt.Errorf(\"invalid entry\")}\n \t\t}\n+\t\tfields = fields[:3]\n \t\tpath := string(record[i+1:])\n \t\tif fields[0] == \"160000\" && matters != nil && !matters(path) {\n \t\t\tcontinue\n@@ -316,20 +389,20 @@ func gitMaterializedChangesForIn(files Files, root, commit string, matters func(\n \t\t\tif runtime.GOOS != \"windows\" && (info.Mode().Perm()&0111 != 0) != (fields[0] == \"100755\") {\n \t\t\t\tchanged = append(changed, path)\n \t\t\t}\n-\t\t\tif info.Size() > (256<<20)-total {\n-\t\t\t\treturn nil, &GitSnapshotError{\"read \" + path, fmt.Errorf(\"snapshot exceeds 256 MiB\")}\n+\t\t\tif info.Size() > budget-total {\n+\t\t\t\treturn nil, &GitSnapshotError{\"read \" + path, fmt.Errorf(\"snapshot exceeds its budget of %d bytes\", budget)}\n \t\t\t}\n \t\t\tvar file *os.File\n \t\t\tfile, e = os.Open(full)\n \t\t\tif e == nil {\n-\t\t\t\traw, e = io.ReadAll(io.LimitReader(file, (256<<20)-total+1))\n+\t\t\t\traw, e = io.ReadAll(io.LimitReader(file, budget-total+1))\n \t\t\t\tcloseErr := file.Close()\n \t\t\t\tif e == nil {\n \t\t\t\t\te = closeErr\n \t\t\t\t}\n \t\t\t\ttotal += int64(len(raw))\n-\t\t\t\tif total > 256<<20 {\n-\t\t\t\t\treturn nil, &GitSnapshotError{\"read \" + path, fmt.Errorf(\"snapshot exceeds 256 MiB\")}\n+\t\t\t\tif total > budget {\n+\t\t\t\t\treturn nil, &GitSnapshotError{\"read \" + path, fmt.Errorf(\"snapshot exceeds its budget of %d bytes\", budget)}\n \t\t\t\t}\n \t\t\t}\n \t\t}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go\nindex 8de5da70..0f1a2fa5 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go\n@@ -441,6 +441,11 @@ type reviewCleanupOwnership struct {\n \tregistration     string\n \tregistrationInfo os.FileInfo\n \tbacklink         string\n+\t// inventoryBytes bounds the bytes the worktree's cleanup may remove: the\n+\t// checked-out commit's tree plus the snapshot margin, read from the\n+\t// coordinator repository when the worktree is registered (spec\n+\t// pose-git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree).\n+\tinventoryBytes int64\n }\n \n func (s Store) captureReviewCleanupOwnership(runtime *os.Root, worktree string, marker []byte) (*reviewCleanupOwnership, error) {\n@@ -463,7 +468,14 @@ func (s Store) captureReviewCleanupOwnership(runtime *os.Root, worktree string,\n \t\tregistry.Close()\n \t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"worktree registration unavailable\")\n \t}\n-\to := &reviewCleanupOwnership{runtime: runtime, registry: registry, registration: name, registrationInfo: info, backlink: filepath.Join(worktree, \".git\")}\n+\to := &reviewCleanupOwnership{runtime: runtime, registry: registry, registration: name, registrationInfo: info, backlink: filepath.Join(worktree, \".git\"), inventoryBytes: gitSnapshotMarginBytes}\n+\tif head, err := registry.ReadFile(filepath.Join(name, \"HEAD\")); err == nil {\n+\t\tif commit := strings.TrimSpace(string(head)); !strings.HasPrefix(commit, \"ref:\") && commit != \"\" {\n+\t\t\tif listing, err := listCommittedTree(s.Root, commit); err == nil {\n+\t\t\t\to.inventoryBytes = gitSnapshotBudget(gitCommittedTreeBytes(listing))\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n \tchild, err := registry.OpenRoot(name)\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\tregistry.Close()\n@@ -554,7 +566,11 @@ func (s Store) cleanupReviewResources(tmp string, owned os.FileInfo, worktree st\n \t\t\t\ttree.Close()\n \t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"worktree cleanup identity changed\")\n \t\t\t}\n-\t\t\te = removeReviewOwnedContents(tree, 100000, 256<<20)\n+\t\t\tlimit := gitSnapshotMarginBytes\n+\t\t\tif o.inventoryBytes > limit {\n+\t\t\t\tlimit = o.inventoryBytes\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\te = removeReviewOwnedContents(tree, 100000, limit)\n \t\t\ttree.Close()\n \t\t\tif e != nil {\n \t\t\t\treturn e\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'cat .pose/specs/*git-snapshot-budget*; cat pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/AGENTS.md; cat locales/pt-BR/AGENTS.md; cat pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/AGENTS.md; cat .pose/rules/backend-go.md; cat .pose/rules/knowledge-governance.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'cat .pose/specs/*git-snapshot-budget*; cat pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/AGENTS.md; cat locales/pt-BR/AGENTS.md; cat pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/AGENTS.md; cat .pose/rules/backend-go.md; cat .pose/rules/knowledge-governance.md'","aggregated_output":"---\nslug: pose-git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree\nstatus: in-progress\ncreated_at: 2026-11-16\ncompleted_at:        # stamped on the transition to status: done\nsupersedes:          # slug of the superseded spec (when applicable)\ndepends_on:          # prerequisites, inline list: other-spec, milestone:<roadmap>/<id>, roadmap:<slug>\nremediates:          # optional explicit links: spec:slug@defect-fix, finding:rva-<16hex>/F1@revert (never inferred from depends_on)\npriority:            # integer >= 0 (lower = higher priority); ordering preference, not a blocker\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: bugfix\nsurface:             # optional: minimal | standard | full (default) — minimal drops Tasks and derivable report sections; `pose specs facts <slug>` derives them\ndelivers: capability:git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree\n---\n\n# Spec: pose-git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\nFazer o orçamento de bytes das capturas de Git que comparam o disco com a árvore commitada crescer com o tamanho dessa árvore, em vez de ficar num teto fixo de 256 MiB.\n\n### Business value\nA árvore commitada do pose-dist passou de 256 MiB (256,8 MiB; 88 MiB de review runs e 102 MiB de review bundles). Desde então, todo `pose close` falha em `gitMaterializedChangesForIn` com \"snapshot exceeds 256 MiB\", e toda revisão delegada falha na limpeza do worktree descartável, que tira um `dispatchDiskSnapshot` do mesmo tamanho. Duas specs aprovadas ou em revisão (`pose-review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation`, `pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph`) ficaram sem poder fechar. As duas capturas precisam ler a árvore inteira para responder; um teto abaixo dela só pode reprovar.\n\n### Constraints\n- Um repositório pequeno não pode ganhar um teto menor que o de hoje.\n- O disco que cresceu além da árvore commitada continua reprovando de forma fechada.\n- Um teto absoluto continua existindo.\n\n### Non-goals\n- Reduzir o tamanho do repositório (retenção de registros de revisão antigos).\n- Mudar o limite de 100.000 entradas.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- R1: `gitMaterializedChangesForIn` and `dispatchDiskSnapshot` shall bound the bytes they read by the committed tree's blob sizes plus a 256 MiB margin, so a clean tree whose checked-out bytes stay within its stored blob bytes plus the margin is compared and snapshotted whole; materialized expansion past that (smudge or CRLF filters, populated submodules, ignored files) fails closed.\n- R2: When the bytes read exceed that budget, both shall fail closed with an error that names the budget.\n- R5: Every committed tree listing these budgets read, with or without a read-view producer, shall be bounded in bytes (64 MiB) and time (2 minutes) before it is retained; a listing past either fails closed.\n- R4: The cleanup of a delegated review's worktree shall bound the bytes it removes by the same budget, computed from the coordinator repository for the worktree's checked-out commit when the worktree is registered, so a clean worktree of a tree past the margin is removed and a worktree grown past the budget is retained.\n- R3: The budget shall never be less than the 256 MiB margin and never more than a 4 GiB ceiling; when the committed tree cannot be listed, the disk snapshot shall use the margin alone.\n\n### Non-functional\n- A listagem da árvore com tamanhos sai do mesmo `ls-tree` que a comparação já fazia; a captura de disco faz um `ls-tree -l` a mais.\n\n### Security\n- O teto absoluto de 4 GiB limita o trabalho de uma captura; o disco que cresceu além da árvore mais a margem continua reprovando.\n\n### Compatibility\n- Para um repositório de até 256 MiB commitados o teto só cresce; nada que passava passa a reprovar.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n- `pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go`: o orçamento das duas capturas.\n- `pose/review_adapter_containment.go`: o inventário da limpeza do worktree da revisão delegada usa o mesmo orçamento.\n\n### Artifacts\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_budget_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go\n- modified: POSE.md\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n- modified: locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n- modified: .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n\n### Delivery targets\n\n- capability:git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n\nComposto em produção pelo `pose close` (passo do plano de fechamento que procura mudanças escondidas) e pela limpeza de toda revisão delegada. Check permanente `git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree-integration`, evidenceClass `integration`, required: `go test ./internal/pose -run 'TestGitSnapshotBudget|TestReviewWorktreeCleanup|TestGitTreeListingIsBounded|TestGovernedTreeListingIsBounded' -count=1`.\n\n### API/contract changes\n- Nenhuma.\n\n### Data/storage changes\n- Nenhuma.\n\n### Technical risks\n- Um repositório acima de 3,75 GiB commitados volta a reprovar no teto; isso fica para uma spec de retenção.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n### Implementation\n- [x] Orçamento escalonado nas duas capturas (R1, R2, R3).\n- [x] Inventário da limpeza do worktree da revisão delegada com o mesmo orçamento (R4).\n\n### Validation\n- [x] Testes com margem reduzida, árvore maior que ela e disco crescido, com prova de reprovação.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Decisions\n\n### Decision D1\n- Date: 2026-11-16\n- Context: o maintainer escolheu, entre escalonar com a árvore, subir a constante para 1 GiB e retenção dos registros de revisão, escalonar com a árvore.\n- Options considered: (a) orçamento proporcional à árvore commitada, com margem e teto; (b) constante fixa de 1 GiB; (c) retenção de registros antigos.\n- Decision: (a), margem de 256 MiB e teto de 4 GiB.\n- Basis: R1, R2, R3\n- Rationale: (b) volta a quebrar quando a árvore passar de 1 GiB; (c) muda dado governado e é mais lenta para destravar; (a) segue o trabalho que a captura precisa fazer e mantém a reprovação para o disco que cresceu.\n- Consequences: o custo de uma captura cresce com o repositório, como já crescia o trabalho necessário.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\nTestes com um repositório real de quatro arquivos de 4 KiB e a margem reduzida a 1 KiB, de modo que a árvore commitada passa da margem, como a do pose-dist passou de 256 MiB.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n#### Test\n- Command: `go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver ./internal/scaffold -count=1`\n- Scope: pose-mcp\n- Expected: verde\n\n### Execution log\n- Date: 2026-11-16\n- Environment: Linux, Go 1.26, Git 2.56.\n- Notes: com o teto antigo (só a margem), o teste da árvore inteira reprova com \"snapshot exceeds its budget of 1024 bytes\"; com o orçamento escalonado passa, e um arquivo que cresce 60 KiB além da árvore reprova nas duas capturas. Os fechamentos de `pose-review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation` e `pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph` reprovaram com \"snapshot exceeds 256 MiB\" sobre a árvore de 256,8 MiB do pose-dist.\n\n### Results summary\n- Successes: as duas capturas cobrem uma árvore maior que a margem e continuam reprovando o disco crescido.\n- Failures: nenhuma.\n- Warnings: nenhum.\n\n### Requirement trace\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestGitSnapshotBudgetCoversTheCommittedTree check:git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree-integration\n- R2 [satisfied] test:TestGitSnapshotBudgetStillBoundsGrowth\n- R3 [satisfied] test:TestGitSnapshotBudgetIsBounded\n- R4 [satisfied] test:TestReviewWorktreeCleanupCoversTheCommittedTree test:TestReviewWorktreeCleanupStillBoundsGrowth\n- R5 [satisfied] test:TestGitTreeListingIsBounded test:TestGovernedTreeListingIsBounded\n\n### Known gaps\n- O caso de a listagem da árvore falhar na captura de disco usa só a margem, sem teste próprio.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\n\nNão concluída.\n\n### Residual risks\n\n### Follow-ups\n\n- [open] F1: decidir a retenção dos registros de revisão, que somam 190 MiB dos 256,8 MiB da árvore do pose-dist e crescem a cada rodada. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-11-30)\n\n### Review\n\nRodada 1 (run rrn-06ad526d19316762, recusada): a revisão terminou, mas a limpeza do worktree descartável falhou com \"runtime cleanup inventory incomplete; resources retained\", e a conclusão foi recusada, como a da rodada 4 do doctor (rrn-f0d738ef7de4226e). A causa era um terceiro teto fixo de 256 MiB, o do inventário que `removeReviewOwnedContents` remove do worktree, um checkout da árvore de 256,8 MiB. Ele passou a usar o mesmo orçamento: ao registrar o worktree, o motor lê o commit destacado do registro e soma a árvore dele no repositório coordenador, sem rodar Git dentro do worktree do revisor (R4). Com o teto fixo, `TestReviewWorktreeCleanupCoversTheCommittedTree` reproduz a mesma mensagem; um worktree que cresce 64 KiB além do orçamento continua retido (`TestReviewWorktreeCleanupStillBoundsGrowth`).\n\nRodada 2 (run rrn-93ce7f7f0467fa87, changes-requested): um bloqueador e dois follow-ups, tratados. N2 as listagens de árvore (`ls-tree -r -l -z`) da captura de disco e do orçamento da limpeza eram retidas inteiras, sem prazo, antes do limite de entradas; agora as três passam por `listCommittedTree`, com 64 MiB e 2 minutos, e uma listagem acima disso reprova fechada nas três (R5, `TestGitTreeListingIsBounded`, que reprova com a listagem sem limite). N1 o R1 prometia cobertura de toda árvore limpa até o teto, mas o orçamento mede bytes armazenados; o R1 passou a dizer que a expansão materializada além da margem reprova fechada. N3 o POSE.md e os dois manuais do scaffold descreviam o inventário do workspace com 256 MiB fixos; agora descrevem os bytes da árvore do commit mais 256 MiB, entre 256 MiB e 4 GiB.\n\nRodada 3 (run rrn-f64458878e6490e0, changes-requested): N1 e N3 corrigidos, N2 parcial, e um bloqueador, N4, corrigido com teste que reprova sem a correção. O fechamento real compara a árvore sob o produtor `closeout-plan`, e esse caminho listava por `captureGovernanceGit`, com o limite de 512 MiB da read view e sem prazo; agora a listagem governada passa por `CaptureGovernanceGitContextIn` com os 64 MiB e os 2 minutos do R5, mantendo a proveniência na read view (`TestGovernedTreeListingIsBounded`, que cobre o limite de bytes e o prazo pelo caminho com produtor, e o prazo pelo caminho sem produtor).\n\n# AGENTS.md — {{PROJECT_NAME}}\n\nThis repository uses **POSE** (Project Operating Standard for Engineering) to\ngovern agent work. This file is the short contract. For the operating manual\n(structure, CLI, per-task-type flows, CI policy), see [`POSE.md`](POSE.md).\n\n## Project context\n\n<!-- pose:instance-owned -->\n\n<!-- Describe here, in 3-6 lines, what this repository is: components,\n     high-level architecture, and where the project's canonical references\n     live (vision, backlog, decisions). Point to subproject AGENTS.md files\n     when they exist. `pose install` excerpts this from an existing\n     README.md/CLAUDE.md on first install when one is present; `pose\n     update` never touches this section afterward — edit it directly. -->\n\n{{PROJECT_NAME}}: describe the repository's purpose and its main components.\n\n## Instruction precedence\n\nOn conflict: (1) direct instruction of the current task; (2) the most specific\n`AGENTS.md` (deepest in the affected directory); (3) the broadest `AGENTS.md`\n(root). Read only the `AGENTS.md` files needed for the paths involved.\n\n## Mandatory artifacts (spec / ADR / checks)\n\n- **Spec**: required for non-trivial feature/scope changes.\n- **ADR**: required for architectural decisions or structural contract changes.\n- **Checks**: required whenever an applicable command exists in the changed\n  module (`test`, `lint`, `typecheck`, `build`, security/contract checks).\n- **Commit trailer (`POSE-Spec:`)**: required on every commit that implements,\n  modifies, or tests artifacts declared by a spec (`POSE-Spec: <slug>`).\n  Without this trailer, `pose artifact-check` and `pose close` cannot attribute\n  Git change sets to the spec's `### Artifacts` section.\n\n  POSE finds this line by scanning the commit message for the `POSE-Spec:`\n  prefix (`allCommitsWithSpecTrailers`). It does not use Git's trailer parser,\n  and nothing in the distribution calls `%(trailers` or `interpret-trailers`.\n  So a `POSE-Spec:` line separated from the rest of the trailer block by a blank\n  line is invisible to `git log --format=%(trailers:...)` and to reviewers that\n  measure with it — one has reported \"no `POSE-Spec:` trailer\" on three\n  consecutive commits that carried it — while POSE attributes it correctly.\n  Keep the block contiguous for git-native tooling and readability; do not\n  conclude that attribution is broken from a reading taken with Git's parser.\n  Confirm with `pose artifact-check --spec <slug>` and compare `claims` against\n  `observed`.\n\n  When attribution really is wrong, the usual cause is the slug rather than the\n  format: a change set resolves as a commit **range**, so every commit carrying\n  the same slug makes it span the whole branch, which is correct behaviour for\n  that input.\n\n## Active paths in the flow\n\n- POSE operating manual: [`POSE.md`](POSE.md)\n- Workflows per task type: [`.pose/workflows/`](.pose/workflows/)\n- Domain rules (cumulative): [`.pose/rules/`](.pose/rules/)\n- Specs per feature/scope: [`.pose/specs/`](.pose/specs/)\n- Governed roadmaps: [`.pose/roadmaps/`](.pose/roadmaps/)\n- Implementation ADRs: [`.pose/adr/`](.pose/adr/)\n- Skills for recurring tasks: [`.agents/skills/`](.agents/skills/)\n- Native automation entrypoint: the `pose` Go binary (`pose help`).\n\n## Assessment Tool Execution Timing\n\nAI agents must use assessment tools at specific points in the flow:\n\n1. **Task / Spec Start (`pose-feature`)**:\n   - Run `pose assess discover --if-stale [--component <dir>]` / `pose_component_discover` before modifying code: a component's assessment is reused while its committed content, the engine and the validation matrix are unchanged, and refreshed otherwise.\n2. **Inter-Module Contract Change / PR Review (`pose-review`)**:\n   - Run `pose assess integrate` / `pose_integration_check` when touching Protobuf, Kafka, REST APIs, or MCP tools.\n   - Run `pose assess tech-debt` / `pose_tech_debt_check` during code review to ensure markers (`TODO`, `FIXME`, `stub`, `panic`) are covered by follow-ups or specs.\n3. **Spec Closure (`pose-spec-closeout`)**:\n   - Run `pose assess discover --if-stale --update-state` upon delivery completion (components the delivery did not change are reused, not rescanned) to recalculate dynamic platform completeness and update `.pose/assessments/` and `.pose/state/`.\n\n## Domain rules\n\nApply the rules relevant to the scope, cumulatively:\n\n- Go backend: shipped as the extension `pose-rule-backend-go` — install with `pose extension install pose-rule-backend-go`.\n- Python backend: shipped as the extension `pose-rule-backend-python` — install with `pose extension install pose-rule-backend-python`.\n- Rust backend: shipped as the extension `pose-rule-backend-rust` — install with `pose extension install pose-rule-backend-rust`.\n- Java/Kotlin backend: shipped as the extension `pose-rule-backend-java` — install with `pose extension install pose-rule-backend-java`.\n- .NET backend: shipped as the extension `pose-rule-backend-dotnet` — install with `pose extension install pose-rule-backend-dotnet`.\n- React frontend: shipped as the extension `pose-rule-frontend-react` — install with `pose extension install pose-rule-frontend-react`.\n- Vue frontend: shipped as the extension `pose-rule-frontend-vue` — install with `pose extension install pose-rule-frontend-vue`.\n- Svelte frontend: shipped as the extension `pose-rule-frontend-svelte` — install with `pose extension install pose-rule-frontend-svelte`.\n- Cloudflare Workers: shipped as the extension `pose-rule-serverless-cloudflare` — install with `pose extension install pose-rule-serverless-cloudflare`.\n- Docker: shipped as the extension `pose-rule-infra-docker` — install with `pose extension install pose-rule-infra-docker`.\n- Terraform: shipped as the extension `pose-rule-infra-terraform` — install with `pose extension install pose-rule-infra-terraform`.\n- Kubernetes: shipped as the reference extension `pose-rule-kubernetes` — install with `pose extension install pose-rule-kubernetes`.\n- GitHub Actions CI/CD: shipped as the extension `pose-rule-cicd-github-actions` — install with `pose extension install pose-rule-cicd-github-actions`.\n- Security: [`.pose/rules/security.md`](.pose/rules/security.md)\n- Documentation / Process: [`.pose/rules/documentation-style.md`](.pose/rules/documentation-style.md)\n- Delivery evidence (claiming delivery requires a gate): [`.pose/rules/delivery-evidence.md`](.pose/rules/delivery-evidence.md)\n- Knowledge governance: [`.pose/rules/knowledge-governance.md`](.pose/rules/knowledge-governance.md)\n\n**Precedence between domains:** on conflict, apply the most restrictive rule\n(usually `security`) without breaking frontend/backend contracts.\n\n## Available skills\n\nUse the skill matching the task type (do not load all of them). Catalog in\n[`.agents/skills/README.md`](.agents/skills/README.md); machine-readable\ndiscovery: `pose suggest <type> [--path <dir>]`.\n\n- `pose-feature` · `pose-bugfix` · `pose-review` · `pose-adr` · `pose-test-plan`\n- `pose-doc-update` · `pose-knowledge` · `pose-spec-closeout` · `pose-recurrence-escalation`\n\n## Verification\n\nPrefer deterministic checks whenever they exist: `test`, `lint`, `typecheck`,\n`build`, security/contract validations. Canonical matrix in\n[`.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json`](.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json),\nexecuted by `pose validate`.\n\n## Do not\n\n- Large refactors unrelated to the task at hand.\n- Change public contracts without updating the applicable spec/ADR/docs.\n- Skip tests when an applicable test command exists in the module.\n- Expose secrets in code, docs, examples or logs.\n\n## Instance notes\n\n<!-- pose:instance-owned -->\n\n<!-- Repository-specific agent guidance. `pose update` refreshes every other\n     section of this file from the shipped contract but never touches this one,\n     so put local conventions, exceptions and pointers here rather than editing\n     the engine-owned sections above. -->\n# AGENTS.md — {{PROJECT_NAME}}\n\nEste repositório usa o **POSE** (Project Operating Standard for Engineering) para orientar\ntrabalho de agentes. Este arquivo é o contrato curto. Para o manual operacional (estrutura,\nCLI, fluxos por tipo de tarefa, política de CI), consulte [`POSE.md`](POSE.md).\n\n## Contexto do projeto\n\n<!-- pose:instance-owned -->\n\n<!-- Descreva aqui, em 3-6 linhas, o que este repositório é: componentes,\n     arquitetura de alto nível e onde vivem as referências canônicas do\n     projeto (visão, backlog, decisões). Aponte AGENTS.md específicos de\n     subprojetos quando existirem. O `pose install` extrai isto de um\n     README.md/CLAUDE.md existente na primeira instalação, quando houver;\n     o `pose update` nunca toca nesta seção depois — edite-a diretamente. -->\n\n{{PROJECT_NAME}}: descreva o propósito do repositório e seus componentes principais.\n\n## Precedência de instruções\n\nEm conflito: (1) instrução direta da tarefa atual; (2) `AGENTS.md` mais específico (mais\nprofundo no diretório afetado); (3) `AGENTS.md` mais abrangente (raiz). Leia apenas os\n`AGENTS.md` necessários para os caminhos envolvidos.\n\n## Obrigatoriedade (spec / ADR / checks)\n\n- **Spec**: obrigatória para mudanças não-triviais de feature/escopo.\n- **ADR**: obrigatória em decisão arquitetural ou alteração de contrato estrutural.\n- **Checks**: obrigatórios quando existir comando aplicável no módulo alterado (`test`,\n  `lint`, `typecheck`, `build`, checks de segurança/contrato).\n- **Trailer de commit (`POSE-Spec:`)**: obrigatório em cada commit que implemente,\n  altere ou teste artefatos declarados em uma spec (`POSE-Spec: <slug>`).\n  Sem esse trailer, o `pose artifact-check` e o `pose close` não conseguem atribuir\n  os change sets do Git à seção `### Artifacts` da spec.\n\n  O POSE encontra essa linha varrendo a mensagem do commit pelo prefixo\n  `POSE-Spec:` (`allCommitsWithSpecTrailers`). Ele **não** usa o parser de\n  trailers do Git, e nada na distribuição chama `%(trailers` ou\n  `interpret-trailers`. Uma linha `POSE-Spec:` separada do resto do bloco por\n  uma linha em branco é, portanto, invisível para `git log\n  --format=%(trailers:...)` e para revisores que medem com ele — um deles\n  reportou \"sem trailer `POSE-Spec:`\" em três commits seguidos que o continham —\n  enquanto o POSE atribui corretamente. Mantenha o bloco contíguo por causa de\n  ferramenta git-native e legibilidade; não conclua que a atribuição quebrou a\n  partir de uma leitura feita com o parser do Git. Confirme com\n  `pose artifact-check --spec <slug>` e compare `claims` com `observed`.\n\n  Quando a atribuição está de fato errada, a causa costuma ser o slug, não o\n  formato: um change set resolve como um **intervalo** de commits, então todos\n  carregando o mesmo slug fazem ele abranger o branch inteiro — comportamento\n  correto para aquela entrada.\n\n## Paths ativos no fluxo\n\n- Manual operacional POSE: [`POSE.md`](POSE.md)\n- Workflows por tipo de tarefa: [`.pose/workflows/`](.pose/workflows/)\n- Rules por domínio (cumulativas): [`.pose/rules/`](.pose/rules/)\n- Specs por feature/escopo: [`.pose/specs/`](.pose/specs/)\n- Roadmaps governados: [`.pose/roadmaps/`](.pose/roadmaps/)\n- ADRs de implementação: [`.pose/adr/`](.pose/adr/)\n- Skills por tarefa recorrente: [`.agents/skills/`](.agents/skills/)\n- Entry point nativo de automação: binário Go `pose` (`pose help`).\n\n## Momento de Execução das Tools de Assessment POSE\n\nAgentes de IA devem utilizar as ferramentas de assessment em momentos específicos do fluxo:\n\n1. **Início de Task / Spec (`pose-feature`)**:\n   - Executar `pose assess discover --if-stale [--component <dir>]` / `pose_component_discover` antes de modificar código: o assessment de um componente é reaproveitado enquanto o conteúdo commitado, o motor e a matriz de validação não mudam, e é refeito caso contrário.\n2. **Alteração de Contrato Inter-Módulo / PR Review (`pose-review`)**:\n   - Executar `pose assess integrate` / `pose_integration_check` quando tocar em Protobuf, Kafka, APIs REST ou ferramentas MCP.\n   - Executar `pose assess tech-debt` / `pose_tech_debt_check` durante code review para garantir que marcadores (`TODO`, `FIXME`, `stub`, `panic`) foram cobertos por follow-ups ou specs.\n3. **Fechamento de Spec (`pose-spec-closeout`)**:\n   - Executar `pose assess discover --if-stale --update-state` ao concluir a entrega (componentes que a entrega não mudou são reaproveitados, não reescaneados) para recalcular a completude dinâmica da plataforma e atualizar `.pose/assessments/` e `.pose/state/`.\n\n## Rules por domínio\n\nAplique cumulativamente as rules relevantes ao escopo:\n\n- Backend Go: distribuída como a extensão `pose-rule-backend-go` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-backend-go`.\n- Backend Python: distribuída como a extensão `pose-rule-backend-python` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-backend-python`.\n- Backend Rust: distribuída como a extensão `pose-rule-backend-rust` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-backend-rust`.\n- Backend Java/Kotlin: distribuída como a extensão `pose-rule-backend-java` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-backend-java`.\n- Backend .NET: distribuída como a extensão `pose-rule-backend-dotnet` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-backend-dotnet`.\n- Frontend React: distribuída como a extensão `pose-rule-frontend-react` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-frontend-react`.\n- Frontend Vue: distribuída como a extensão `pose-rule-frontend-vue` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-frontend-vue`.\n- Frontend Svelte: distribuída como a extensão `pose-rule-frontend-svelte` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-frontend-svelte`.\n- Cloudflare Workers: distribuída como a extensão `pose-rule-serverless-cloudflare` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-serverless-cloudflare`.\n- Docker: distribuída como a extensão `pose-rule-infra-docker` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-infra-docker`.\n- Terraform: distribuída como a extensão `pose-rule-infra-terraform` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-infra-terraform`.\n- Kubernetes: distribuída como a extensão de referência `pose-rule-kubernetes` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-kubernetes`.\n- CI/CD GitHub Actions: distribuída como a extensão `pose-rule-cicd-github-actions` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-cicd-github-actions`.\n- Security: [`.pose/rules/security.md`](.pose/rules/security.md)\n- Documentation / Process: [`.pose/rules/documentation-style.md`](.pose/rules/documentation-style.md)\n- Delivery evidence (declarar entrega exige gate): [`.pose/rules/delivery-evidence.md`](.pose/rules/delivery-evidence.md)\n- Knowledge governance: [`.pose/rules/knowledge-governance.md`](.pose/rules/knowledge-governance.md)\n\n**Precedência entre domínios:** em conflito, aplique a regra mais restritiva (normalmente\n`security`) sem quebrar contratos de frontend/backend.\n\n## Skills disponíveis\n\nUse a skill correspondente ao tipo de tarefa (não carregue todas). Catálogo em\n[`.agents/skills/README.md`](.agents/skills/README.md); descoberta machine-readable:\n`pose suggest <tipo> [--path <dir>]`.\n\n- `pose-feature` · `pose-bugfix` · `pose-review` · `pose-adr` · `pose-test-plan`\n- `pose-doc-update` · `pose-knowledge` · `pose-spec-closeout` · `pose-recurrence-escalation`\n\n## Verificação\n\nPrefira checks determinísticos quando existirem: `test`, `lint`, `typecheck`, `build`,\nvalidações de segurança/contrato. Matriz canônica em\n[`.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json`](.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json), executada\npor `pose validate`.\n\n## Não fazer\n\n- Refactors grandes e não relacionados à tarefa.\n- Alterar contratos públicos sem atualizar spec/ADR/docs aplicáveis.\n- Pular testes quando existir comando de teste aplicável no módulo.\n- Expor segredos em código, docs, exemplos ou logs.\n\n## Notas da instância\n\n<!-- pose:instance-owned -->\n\n<!-- Orientação para agentes específica deste repositório. O `pose update`\n     atualiza todas as outras seções deste arquivo a partir do contrato\n     distribuído, mas nunca toca nesta — registre aqui convenções locais,\n     exceções e ponteiros, em vez de editar as seções do motor acima. -->\n# AGENTS.md — {{PROJECT_NAME}}\n\nEste repositório usa o **POSE** (Project Operating Standard for Engineering) para orientar\ntrabalho de agentes. Este arquivo é o contrato curto. Para o manual operacional (estrutura,\nCLI, fluxos por tipo de tarefa, política de CI), consulte [`POSE.md`](POSE.md).\n\n## Contexto do projeto\n\n<!-- pose:instance-owned -->\n\n<!-- Descreva aqui, em 3-6 linhas, o que este repositório é: componentes,\n     arquitetura de alto nível e onde vivem as referências canônicas do\n     projeto (visão, backlog, decisões). Aponte AGENTS.md específicos de\n     subprojetos quando existirem. O `pose install` extrai isto de um\n     README.md/CLAUDE.md existente na primeira instalação, quando houver;\n     o `pose update` nunca toca nesta seção depois — edite-a diretamente. -->\n\n{{PROJECT_NAME}}: descreva o propósito do repositório e seus componentes principais.\n\n## Precedência de instruções\n\nEm conflito: (1) instrução direta da tarefa atual; (2) `AGENTS.md` mais específico (mais\nprofundo no diretório afetado); (3) `AGENTS.md` mais abrangente (raiz). Leia apenas os\n`AGENTS.md` necessários para os caminhos envolvidos.\n\n## Obrigatoriedade (spec / ADR / checks)\n\n- **Spec**: obrigatória para mudanças não-triviais de feature/escopo.\n- **ADR**: obrigatória em decisão arquitetural ou alteração de contrato estrutural.\n- **Checks**: obrigatórios quando existir comando aplicável no módulo alterado (`test`,\n  `lint`, `typecheck`, `build`, checks de segurança/contrato).\n- **Trailer de commit (`POSE-Spec:`)**: obrigatório em cada commit que implemente,\n  altere ou teste artefatos declarados em uma spec (`POSE-Spec: <slug>`).\n  Sem esse trailer, o `pose artifact-check` e o `pose close` não conseguem atribuir\n  os change sets do Git à seção `### Artifacts` da spec.\n\n  O POSE encontra essa linha varrendo a mensagem do commit pelo prefixo\n  `POSE-Spec:` (`allCommitsWithSpecTrailers`). Ele **não** usa o parser de\n  trailers do Git, e nada na distribuição chama `%(trailers` ou\n  `interpret-trailers`. Uma linha `POSE-Spec:` separada do resto do bloco por\n  uma linha em branco é, portanto, invisível para `git log\n  --format=%(trailers:...)` e para revisores que medem com ele — um deles\n  reportou \"sem trailer `POSE-Spec:`\" em três commits seguidos que o continham —\n  enquanto o POSE atribui corretamente. Mantenha o bloco contíguo por causa de\n  ferramenta git-native e legibilidade; não conclua que a atribuição quebrou a\n  partir de uma leitura feita com o parser do Git. Confirme com\n  `pose artifact-check --spec <slug>` e compare `claims` com `observed`.\n\n  Quando a atribuição está de fato errada, a causa costuma ser o slug, não o\n  formato: um change set resolve como um **intervalo** de commits, então todos\n  carregando o mesmo slug fazem ele abranger o branch inteiro — comportamento\n  correto para aquela entrada.\n\n## Paths ativos no fluxo\n\n- Manual operacional POSE: [`POSE.md`](POSE.md)\n- Workflows por tipo de tarefa: [`.pose/workflows/`](.pose/workflows/)\n- Rules por domínio (cumulativas): [`.pose/rules/`](.pose/rules/)\n- Specs por feature/escopo: [`.pose/specs/`](.pose/specs/)\n- Roadmaps governados: [`.pose/roadmaps/`](.pose/roadmaps/)\n- ADRs de implementação: [`.pose/adr/`](.pose/adr/)\n- Skills por tarefa recorrente: [`.agents/skills/`](.agents/skills/)\n- Entry point nativo de automação: binário Go `pose` (`pose help`).\n\n## Momento de Execução das Tools de Assessment POSE\n\nAgentes de IA devem utilizar as ferramentas de assessment em momentos específicos do fluxo:\n\n1. **Início de Task / Spec (`pose-feature`)**:\n   - Executar `pose assess discover --if-stale [--component <dir>]` / `pose_component_discover` antes de modificar código: o assessment de um componente é reaproveitado enquanto o conteúdo commitado, o motor e a matriz de validação não mudam, e é refeito caso contrário.\n2. **Alteração de Contrato Inter-Módulo / PR Review (`pose-review`)**:\n   - Executar `pose assess integrate` / `pose_integration_check` quando tocar em Protobuf, Kafka, APIs REST ou ferramentas MCP.\n   - Executar `pose assess tech-debt` / `pose_tech_debt_check` durante code review para garantir que marcadores (`TODO`, `FIXME`, `stub`, `panic`) foram cobertos por follow-ups ou specs.\n3. **Fechamento de Spec (`pose-spec-closeout`)**:\n   - Executar `pose assess discover --if-stale --update-state` ao concluir a entrega (componentes que a entrega não mudou são reaproveitados, não reescaneados) para recalcular a completude dinâmica da plataforma e atualizar `.pose/assessments/` e `.pose/state/`.\n\n## Rules por domínio\n\nAplique cumulativamente as rules relevantes ao escopo:\n\n- Backend Go: distribuída como a extensão `pose-rule-backend-go` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-backend-go`.\n- Backend Python: distribuída como a extensão `pose-rule-backend-python` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-backend-python`.\n- Backend Rust: distribuída como a extensão `pose-rule-backend-rust` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-backend-rust`.\n- Backend Java/Kotlin: distribuída como a extensão `pose-rule-backend-java` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-backend-java`.\n- Backend .NET: distribuída como a extensão `pose-rule-backend-dotnet` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-backend-dotnet`.\n- Frontend React: distribuída como a extensão `pose-rule-frontend-react` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-frontend-react`.\n- Frontend Vue: distribuída como a extensão `pose-rule-frontend-vue` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-frontend-vue`.\n- Frontend Svelte: distribuída como a extensão `pose-rule-frontend-svelte` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-frontend-svelte`.\n- Cloudflare Workers: distribuída como a extensão `pose-rule-serverless-cloudflare` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-serverless-cloudflare`.\n- Docker: distribuída como a extensão `pose-rule-infra-docker` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-infra-docker`.\n- Terraform: distribuída como a extensão `pose-rule-infra-terraform` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-infra-terraform`.\n- Kubernetes: distribuída como a extensão de referência `pose-rule-kubernetes` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-kubernetes`.\n- CI/CD GitHub Actions: distribuída como a extensão `pose-rule-cicd-github-actions` — instale com `pose extension install pose-rule-cicd-github-actions`.\n- Security: [`.pose/rules/security.md`](.pose/rules/security.md)\n- Documentation / Process: [`.pose/rules/documentation-style.md`](.pose/rules/documentation-style.md)\n- Delivery evidence (declarar entrega exige gate): [`.pose/rules/delivery-evidence.md`](.pose/rules/delivery-evidence.md)\n- Knowledge governance: [`.pose/rules/knowledge-governance.md`](.pose/rules/knowledge-governance.md)\n\n**Precedência entre domínios:** em conflito, aplique a regra mais restritiva (normalmente\n`security`) sem quebrar contratos de frontend/backend.\n\n## Skills disponíveis\n\nUse a skill correspondente ao tipo de tarefa (não carregue todas). Catálogo em\n[`.agents/skills/README.md`](.agents/skills/README.md); descoberta machine-readable:\n`pose suggest <tipo> [--path <dir>]`.\n\n- `pose-feature` · `pose-bugfix` · `pose-review` · `pose-adr` · `pose-test-plan`\n- `pose-doc-update` · `pose-knowledge` · `pose-spec-closeout` · `pose-recurrence-escalation`\n\n## Verificação\n\nPrefira checks determinísticos quando existirem: `test`, `lint`, `typecheck`, `build`,\nvalidações de segurança/contrato. Matriz canônica em\n[`.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json`](.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json), executada\npor `pose validate`.\n\n## Não fazer\n\n- Refactors grandes e não relacionados à tarefa.\n- Alterar contratos públicos sem atualizar spec/ADR/docs aplicáveis.\n- Pular testes quando existir comando de teste aplicável no módulo.\n- Expor segredos em código, docs, exemplos ou logs.\n\n## Notas da instância\n\n<!-- pose:instance-owned -->\n\n<!-- Orientação para agentes específica deste repositório. O `pose update`\n     atualiza todas as outras seções deste arquivo a partir do contrato\n     distribuído, mas nunca toca nesta — registre aqui convenções locais,\n     exceções e ponteiros, em vez de editar as seções do motor acima. -->\n# Rule: Backend Go\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide for HTTP handlers, domain services, persistence, concurrency, and integrations between Go services.\n\n## Required patterns\n\n- Handle and propagate errors with enough context for diagnosis.\n- Validate handler input and return HTTP status codes consistent with the contract.\n- Keep business rules in service or domain layers, not in transport code.\n- Honor `context.Context` for timeouts and cancellation.\n- Put data access behind clear interfaces that support testing.\n- Use structured logs without exposing sensitive data.\n\n## Blocking anti-patterns\n\n- Ignoring error returns, including `_` for critical errors.\n- Using `panic` in ordinary request flows instead of controlled error handling.\n- Coupling handlers directly to concrete repository implementations without an abstraction.\n- Running unbounded or unpaginated queries in potentially large endpoints.\n- Introducing concurrency without adequate synchronization or race protection.\n\n## Minimum checks\n\n- Run `go test ./...` in the affected scope.\n- Run `go test -race ./...` when concurrency changes.\n- Run `go vet ./...` without blocking findings.\n- Run the applicable Go lint check, such as `golangci-lint`, without critical errors.\n\n## Precedence in multi-domain conflicts\n\n- Apply the most restrictive security, contract, and operational rule when domain rules conflict.\n- Prefer verifiable check evidence and explicit risk mitigation when speed conflicts with control.\n- Record the precedence decision and objective rationale in the review.\n\n## Recurrence traceability\n\n> Also apply: [.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md](_base-recurrence.md)\n# Rule: Knowledge Governance\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide when creating, updating, reviewing, or removing artifacts under `.pose/knowledge/`.\n\n## TTL and retention\n\n- Set `expires_at` on every artifact when it is created.\n- Use a default TTL of 30 days for notes, decision logs, and handoffs.\n- Use a TTL of up to 90 days only with a justification recorded in the artifact body.\n- Treat an artifact without `expires_at` as non-compliant and block its creation or merge.\n\n## When this is not the right home\n\n- Use `.pose/knowledge/` only for time-bound operational memory: content\n  tied to a decision moment, a handoff between executions, or something\n  meant to be reviewed and eventually expire.\n- A durable fact or convention that will not become false and carries no\n  review trigger — a third-party tool's parsing quirk, a naming\n  convention, a recurring gotcha — is not a `decision-log` just because no\n  better type exists. Route it to `.pose/rules/` instead: add it to an\n  existing rule file or create one, then wire it into the relevant task\n  type's base `rules` array in `.pose/indexes/task-map.json` so\n  `pose suggest <task>` surfaces it automatically. No path scoping is\n  required — a task type's base `rules` list is returned regardless of\n  `--path`; only language/component-specific rules need the\n  `rules_by_domain` layer.\n- Rule of thumb: if nothing was decided or traded off, and nothing about\n  the fact will change on a predictable timeline, it is not a\n  `decision-log` and not an ADR — it is a rule. See ADR\n  `2026-08-15-durable-non-architectural-knowledge-belongs-in-rules-not-a-new-type`.\n\n## Reusable cross-execution format\n\n- Structure reusable context as a handoff with fixed sections: Context, Current state, Next checks, Risks, and Next owner.\n- Keep `source_refs` linked to the relevant spec, workflow, and executed check commands.\n- Record `last_reviewed_at` in the body to make effective cross-execution updates traceable.\n\n## Archiving and purging\n\n- Run biweekly triage to list expired artifacts.\n- Move expired artifacts to `.pose/knowledge/archive/` when they retain audit value.\n- Purge archived artifacts 180 days after expiration unless documented legal or compliance requirements apply.\n- Record every archive and purge action in the housekeeping log.\n\n## Sensitive content\n\n- Prohibit secrets, tokens, credentials, private keys, and equivalent material.\n- Prohibit personal data and non-anonymized customer data.\n- Do not copy restricted incidents or reports in full; keep only a controlled reference.\n- Classify frontmatter `sensitivity` as `public-internal` or `restricted`.\n- Remove identified sensitive content immediately and open a security follow-up.\n\n## Ownership and review\n\n- Keep `@pose-maintainers` as the primary governance owner.\n- Require an owner in every artifact frontmatter.\n- Review expiration biweekly and quality monthly.\n- Escalate a backlog overdue by more than two cycles to the primary owner.\n- Block backlog growth when `list-expired` exceeds the operational limit: zero in strict mode, two in tolerant mode.\n\n## Minimum operational checks\n\n- Run `pose knowledge-check --strict` biweekly to validate the expired backlog.\n- Run `pose knowledge-housekeeping list-expired` for detailed triage.\n- Run `pose knowledge-housekeeping archive-expired --dry-run` before applying changes.\n- Execute destructive actions only with an explicit `--apply` flag.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go | head -460; cat /var/tmp/closeout/ac-bg.out /var/tmp/closeout/sc-bg.out'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go | head -460; cat /var/tmp/closeout/ac-bg.out /var/tmp/closeout/sc-bg.out'","aggregated_output":"     1\tpackage pose\n     2\t\n     3\timport (\n     4\t\t\"bytes\"\n     5\t\t\"context\"\n     6\t\t\"crypto/sha1\"\n     7\t\t\"crypto/sha256\"\n     8\t\t\"encoding/hex\"\n     9\t\t\"errors\"\n    10\t\t\"fmt\"\n    11\t\t\"hash\"\n    12\t\t\"io\"\n    13\t\t\"io/fs\"\n    14\t\t\"os\"\n    15\t\t\"os/exec\"\n    16\t\t\"path\"\n    17\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n    18\t\t\"runtime\"\n    19\t\t\"sort\"\n    20\t\t\"strconv\"\n    21\t\t\"strings\"\n    22\t\t\"time\"\n    23\t)\n    24\t\n    25\t// The bytes a snapshot reads are bounded by the committed tree it compares\n    26\t// against plus a margin, never less than the margin alone and never more than\n    27\t// the ceiling: a fixed bound stopped every closeout once a repository's\n    28\t// committed tree outgrew it (spec pose-git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree).\n    29\tvar (\n    30\t\tgitSnapshotMarginBytes  int64 = 256 << 20\n    31\t\tgitSnapshotCeilingBytes int64 = 4 << 30\n    32\t)\n    33\t\n    34\tfunc gitSnapshotBudget(committedBytes int64) int64 {\n    35\t\tif committedBytes < 0 {\n    36\t\t\tcommittedBytes = 0\n    37\t\t}\n    38\t\tif committedBytes > gitSnapshotCeilingBytes-gitSnapshotMarginBytes {\n    39\t\t\treturn gitSnapshotCeilingBytes\n    40\t\t}\n    41\t\treturn committedBytes + gitSnapshotMarginBytes\n    42\t}\n    43\t\n    44\t// A committed tree listing is read through a bounded buffer under a\n    45\t// deadline: 100,000 entries of ordinary paths fit well inside it, and a\n    46\t// listing past it fails closed before it is retained (review N2).\n    47\tvar (\n    48\t\tgitTreeListingMaxBytes int64 = 64 << 20\n    49\t\tgitTreeListingTimeout        = 2 * time.Minute\n    50\t)\n    51\t\n    52\t// listCommittedTree returns `ls-tree -r -l -z commit` of root, bounded.\n    53\tfunc listCommittedTree(root, commit string) ([]byte, error) {\n    54\t\tctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), gitTreeListingTimeout)\n    55\t\tdefer cancel()\n    56\t\treturn runGovernanceGitCommandContext(ctx, NativeFiles(), root, []string{\"ls-tree\", \"-r\", \"-l\", \"-z\", commit}, gitTreeListingMaxBytes)\n    57\t}\n    58\t\n    59\t// gitCommittedTreeBytes sums the blob sizes of an `ls-tree -r -l -z` listing.\n    60\tfunc gitCommittedTreeBytes(listing []byte) int64 {\n    61\t\tvar total int64\n    62\t\tfor _, record := range bytes.Split(listing, []byte{0}) {\n    63\t\t\ti := bytes.IndexByte(record, '\\t')\n    64\t\t\tif i < 0 {\n    65\t\t\t\tcontinue\n    66\t\t\t}\n    67\t\t\tfields := strings.Fields(string(record[:i]))\n    68\t\t\tif len(fields) == 4 {\n    69\t\t\t\tif size, err := strconv.ParseInt(fields[3], 10, 64); err == nil && size > 0 {\n    70\t\t\t\t\ttotal += size\n    71\t\t\t\t}\n    72\t\t\t}\n    73\t\t}\n    74\t\treturn total\n    75\t}\n    76\t\n    77\t// Snapshot disk, including ignored files. Git status alone cannot witness\n    78\t// creation of an ignored output. WalkDir never follows a directory symlink.\n    79\tfunc dispatchDiskSnapshot(root string) (map[string]string, error) {\n    80\t\tentries := map[string]string{}\n    81\t\tvar total int64\n    82\t\tcommitted := int64(0)\n    83\t\tif listing, err := listCommittedTree(root, \"HEAD\"); err == nil {\n    84\t\t\tcommitted = gitCommittedTreeBytes(listing)\n    85\t\t}\n    86\t\tbudget := gitSnapshotBudget(committed)\n    87\t\terr := filepath.WalkDir(root, func(path string, entry fs.DirEntry, err error) error {\n    88\t\t\tif err != nil {\n    89\t\t\t\treturn err\n    90\t\t\t}\n    91\t\t\trel, err := filepath.Rel(root, path)\n    92\t\t\tif err != nil {\n    93\t\t\t\treturn err\n    94\t\t\t}\n    95\t\t\tif rel == \".\" {\n    96\t\t\t\treturn nil\n    97\t\t\t}\n    98\t\t\tif rel == \".git\" {\n    99\t\t\t\tif entry.IsDir() {\n   100\t\t\t\t\treturn filepath.SkipDir\n   101\t\t\t\t}\n   102\t\t\t\treturn nil\n   103\t\t\t}\n   104\t\t\tinfo, err := entry.Info()\n   105\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   106\t\t\t\treturn err\n   107\t\t\t}\n   108\t\t\t// The per-root authority lock is runtime coordination state, not a\n   109\t\t\t// project input. Ignore only the exact regular file: a linked or special\n   110\t\t\t// replacement remains visible to the snapshot and fails closed.\n   111\t\t\tif filepath.ToSlash(rel) == \".pose/transfers/.authority-transfer.lock\" && info.Mode().IsRegular() {\n   112\t\t\t\treturn nil\n   113\t\t\t}\n   114\t\t\tif len(entries) >= 100000 {\n   115\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"disk snapshot exceeds 100000 entries\")\n   116\t\t\t}\n   117\t\t\thash := sha256.New()\n   118\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(hash, \"%s\\x00\", info.Mode().String())\n   119\t\t\tswitch {\n   120\t\t\tcase info.Mode().IsRegular():\n   121\t\t\t\tfile, err := os.Open(path)\n   122\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   123\t\t\t\t\treturn err\n   124\t\t\t\t}\n   125\t\t\t\tn, readErr := io.Copy(hash, io.LimitReader(file, budget-total+1))\n   126\t\t\t\tcloseErr := file.Close()\n   127\t\t\t\ttotal += n\n   128\t\t\t\tif readErr != nil {\n   129\t\t\t\t\treturn readErr\n   130\t\t\t\t}\n   131\t\t\t\tif closeErr != nil {\n   132\t\t\t\t\treturn closeErr\n   133\t\t\t\t}\n   134\t\t\t\tif total > budget {\n   135\t\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"disk snapshot exceeds its budget of %d bytes\", budget)\n   136\t\t\t\t}\n   137\t\t\tcase info.Mode()&os.ModeSymlink != 0:\n   138\t\t\t\ttarget, err := os.Readlink(path)\n   139\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   140\t\t\t\t\treturn err\n   141\t\t\t\t}\n   142\t\t\t\thash.Write([]byte(target))\n   143\t\t\tcase info.IsDir():\n   144\t\t\tdefault:\n   145\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"unsupported file type at %q\", rel)\n   146\t\t\t}\n   147\t\t\tentries[filepath.ToSlash(rel)] = hex.EncodeToString(hash.Sum(nil))\n   148\t\t\treturn nil\n   149\t\t})\n   150\t\tif err != nil {\n   151\t\t\treturn nil, &GitSnapshotError{\"disk snapshot\", err}\n   152\t\t}\n   153\t\treturn entries, nil\n   154\t}\n   155\t\n   156\t// GitSnapshotError means a repository observation was unavailable, not clean.\n   157\ttype GitSnapshotError struct {\n   158\t\tOperation string\n   159\t\tCause     error\n   160\t}\n   161\t\n   162\tfunc (e *GitSnapshotError) Error() string {\n   163\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"pose: Git snapshot unavailable (%s): %v\", e.Operation, e.Cause)\n   164\t}\n   165\tfunc (e *GitSnapshotError) Unwrap() error { return e.Cause }\n   166\t\n   167\tfunc snapshotGit(root string, args ...string) ([]byte, error) {\n   168\t\tcmd := gitCommand(append([]string{\"-C\", root}, args...)...)\n   169\t\t// Asking about the worktree writes nothing under .git: without this `git status` refreshes\n   170\t\t// and rewrites the index, which a governed read view that watches .git reads as an input that\n   171\t\t// changed during the operation (spec pose-git-status-leaves-the-git-directory-alone).\n   172\t\tcmd.Env = append(cmd.Env, \"GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0\")\n   173\t\tout, err := cmd.Output()\n   174\t\tif err != nil {\n   175\t\t\treturn nil, &GitSnapshotError{Operation: strings.Join(args, \" \"), Cause: err}\n   176\t\t}\n   177\t\treturn out, nil\n   178\t}\n   179\t\n   180\t// gitChangedPaths uses the NUL protocol; porcelain's quoted display is not a path.\n   181\tfunc gitChangedPaths(root string) ([]string, error) {\n   182\t\tout, err := snapshotGit(root, \"status\", \"--porcelain=v1\", \"-z\", \"--untracked-files=all\", \"--ignore-submodules=none\")\n   183\t\tif err != nil {\n   184\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   185\t\t}\n   186\t\tentries, err := parseGitStatusEntries(out)\n   187\t\tif err != nil {\n   188\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   189\t\t}\n   190\t\tpaths := make([]string, 0, len(entries)*2)\n   191\t\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n   192\t\t\tif untrackedAuthorityTransferLock(entry) {\n   193\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   194\t\t\t}\n   195\t\t\tpaths = append(paths, entry.Path)\n   196\t\t\tif entry.OrigPath != \"\" {\n   197\t\t\t\tpaths = append(paths, entry.OrigPath)\n   198\t\t\t}\n   199\t\t}\n   200\t\tsort.Strings(paths)\n   201\t\treturn paths, nil\n   202\t}\n   203\t\n   204\tfunc untrackedAuthorityTransferLock(entry GitStatusEntry) bool {\n   205\t\treturn entry.XY == \"??\" && entry.Path == \".pose/transfers/.authority-transfer.lock\"\n   206\t}\n   207\t\n   208\tfunc parseGitChangedPaths(out []byte) ([]string, error) {\n   209\t\tentries, err := parseGitStatusEntries(out)\n   210\t\tif err != nil {\n   211\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   212\t\t}\n   213\t\tpaths := []string{}\n   214\t\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n   215\t\t\tpaths = append(paths, entry.Path)\n   216\t\t\tif entry.OrigPath != \"\" {\n   217\t\t\t\tpaths = append(paths, entry.OrigPath)\n   218\t\t\t}\n   219\t\t}\n   220\t\tsort.Strings(paths)\n   221\t\treturn paths, nil\n   222\t}\n   223\t\n   224\t// gitMaterializedChanges checks the committed tree against disk independently\n   225\t// of index flags. No refresh/update-index mutation is needed to see hidden edits.\n   226\tfunc gitMaterializedChanges(root, commit string) ([]string, error) {\n   227\t\treturn gitMaterializedChangesFor(root, commit, nil)\n   228\t}\n   229\tfunc gitMaterializedChangesFor(root, commit string, matters func(string) bool) ([]string, error) {\n   230\t\treturn gitMaterializedChangesForIn(NativeFiles(), root, commit, matters, \"\")\n   231\t}\n   232\t\n   233\tfunc gitMaterializedChangesForIn(files Files, root, commit string, matters func(string) bool, producer string) ([]string, error) {\n   234\t\tfiles = FilesOrNative(files)\n   235\t\tif producer != \"\" {\n   236\t\t\tproducer = governanceProducerFromFiles(files, producer)\n   237\t\t}\n   238\t\trunGit := func(root string, args ...string) ([]byte, error) {\n   239\t\t\tif len(args) == 5 && args[0] == \"ls-tree\" {\n   240\t\t\t\treturn listCommittedTree(root, args[4])\n   241\t\t\t}\n   242\t\t\treturn snapshotGit(root, args...)\n   243\t\t}\n   244\t\tworktreeIdentity := dispatchWorktreeIdentity\n   245\t\tif producer != \"\" {\n   246\t\t\trunGit = func(root string, args ...string) ([]byte, error) {\n   247\t\t\t\tif len(args) == 5 && args[0] == \"ls-tree\" {\n   248\t\t\t\t\t// The governed listing keeps its read-view provenance under the\n   249\t\t\t\t\t// listing's own bound and deadline (review N4).\n   250\t\t\t\t\tctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), gitTreeListingTimeout)\n   251\t\t\t\t\tdefer cancel()\n   252\t\t\t\t\treturn CaptureGovernanceGitContextIn(files, ctx, root, producer, gitTreeListingMaxBytes, args...)\n   253\t\t\t\t}\n   254\t\t\t\treturn captureGovernanceGit(files, root, producer, args...)\n   255\t\t\t}\n   256\t\t\tworktreeIdentity = func(root string) (string, error) {\n   257\t\t\t\treturn dispatchWorktreeIdentityGoverned(files, root, producer)\n   258\t\t\t}\n   259\t\t}\n   260\t\tvar err error\n   261\t\troot, err = filepath.Abs(root)\n   262\t\tif err != nil {\n   263\t\t\treturn nil, &GitSnapshotError{\"root\", err}\n   264\t\t}\n   265\t\tif _, err := worktreeIdentity(root); err != nil {\n   266\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   267\t\t}\n   268\t\tout, err := runGit(root, \"ls-tree\", \"-r\", \"-l\", \"-z\", commit)\n   269\t\tif err != nil {\n   270\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   271\t\t}\n   272\t\tbudget := gitSnapshotBudget(gitCommittedTreeBytes(out))\n   273\t\tvar changed []string\n   274\t\tvar total int64\n   275\t\tcount := 0\n   276\t\tfor _, record := range bytes.Split(out, []byte{0}) {\n   277\t\t\tif len(record) == 0 {\n   278\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   279\t\t\t}\n   280\t\t\tcount++\n   281\t\t\tif count > 100000 {\n   282\t\t\t\treturn nil, &GitSnapshotError{\"tree snapshot\", fmt.Errorf(\"exceeds 100000 entries\")}\n   283\t\t\t}\n   284\t\t\ti := bytes.IndexByte(record, '\\t')\n   285\t\t\tif i < 0 {\n   286\t\t\t\treturn nil, &GitSnapshotError{\"tree protocol\", fmt.Errorf(\"missing path\")}\n   287\t\t\t}\n   288\t\t\tfields := strings.Fields(string(record[:i]))\n   289\t\t\tif len(fields) != 4 {\n   290\t\t\t\treturn nil, &GitSnapshotError{\"tree protocol\", fmt.Errorf(\"invalid entry\")}\n   291\t\t\t}\n   292\t\t\tfields = fields[:3]\n   293\t\t\tpath := string(record[i+1:])\n   294\t\t\tif fields[0] == \"160000\" && matters != nil && !matters(path) {\n   295\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   296\t\t\t}\n   297\t\t\tfull := filepath.Join(root, filepath.FromSlash(path))\n   298\t\t\t// Lstat every parent: a link in a parent must never read outside root.\n   299\t\t\tunsafe := false\n   300\t\t\tfor parent := filepath.Dir(full); parent != root; parent = filepath.Dir(parent) {\n   301\t\t\t\tif parent == filepath.Dir(parent) {\n   302\t\t\t\t\treturn nil, &GitSnapshotError{\"path\", fmt.Errorf(\"path outside worktree: %q\", path)}\n   303\t\t\t\t}\n   304\t\t\t\tvar info os.FileInfo\n   305\t\t\t\tvar e error\n   306\t\t\t\tif producer != \"\" {\n   307\t\t\t\t\tinfo, e = files.Lstat(parent)\n   308\t\t\t\t} else {\n   309\t\t\t\t\tinfo, e = os.Lstat(parent)\n   310\t\t\t\t}\n   311\t\t\t\tif e != nil || !info.IsDir() {\n   312\t\t\t\t\tunsafe = true\n   313\t\t\t\t\tbreak\n   314\t\t\t\t}\n   315\t\t\t}\n   316\t\t\tif unsafe {\n   317\t\t\t\tchanged = append(changed, path)\n   318\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   319\t\t\t}\n   320\t\t\tvar info os.FileInfo\n   321\t\t\tvar e error\n   322\t\t\tif producer != \"\" {\n   323\t\t\t\tinfo, e = files.Lstat(full)\n   324\t\t\t} else {\n   325\t\t\t\tinfo, e = os.Lstat(full)\n   326\t\t\t}\n   327\t\t\tif os.IsNotExist(e) {\n   328\t\t\t\tchanged = append(changed, path)\n   329\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   330\t\t\t}\n   331\t\t\tif e != nil {\n   332\t\t\t\treturn nil, &GitSnapshotError{\"lstat \" + path, e}\n   333\t\t\t}\n   334\t\t\tif fields[0] == \"160000\" {\n   335\t\t\t\tif !info.nl: write error: Broken pipe\nIsDir() {\n   336\t\t\t\t\tchanged = append(changed, path)\n   337\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   338\t\t\t\t}\n   339\t\t\t\tif _, err := worktreeIdentity(full); err != nil {\n   340\t\t\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   341\t\t\t\t}\n   342\t\t\t\thead, e := runGit(full, \"rev-parse\", \"--verify\", \"HEAD\")\n   343\t\t\t\tif e != nil {\n   344\t\t\t\t\treturn nil, e\n   345\t\t\t\t}\n   346\t\t\t\tvar dirty []string\n   347\t\t\t\tif producer != \"\" {\n   348\t\t\t\t\tdirty, e = gitChangedPathsGovernedIn(files, full, producer)\n   349\t\t\t\t} else {\n   350\t\t\t\t\tdirty, e = gitChangedPaths(full)\n   351\t\t\t\t}\n   352\t\t\t\tif e != nil {\n   353\t\t\t\t\treturn nil, e\n   354\t\t\t\t}\n   355\t\t\t\tif strings.TrimSpace(string(head)) != fields[2] || len(dirty) != 0 {\n   356\t\t\t\t\tchanged = append(changed, path)\n   357\t\t\t\t} else {\n   358\t\t\t\t\tvar nested []string\n   359\t\t\t\t\tif producer != \"\" {\n   360\t\t\t\t\t\tnested, err = gitMaterializedChangesForIn(files, full, fields[2], matters, producer)\n   361\t\t\t\t\t} else {\n   362\t\t\t\t\t\tnested, err = gitMaterializedChanges(full, fields[2])\n   363\t\t\t\t\t}\n   364\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   365\t\t\t\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   366\t\t\t\t\t}\n   367\t\t\t\t\tif len(nested) != 0 {\n   368\t\t\t\t\t\tchanged = append(changed, path)\n   369\t\t\t\t\t}\n   370\t\t\t\t}\n   371\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   372\t\t\t}\n   373\t\t\tvar raw []byte\n   374\t\t\tif fields[0] == \"120000\" {\n   375\t\t\t\tif info.Mode()&os.ModeSymlink == 0 {\n   376\t\t\t\t\tchanged = append(changed, path)\n   377\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   378\t\t\t\t}\n   379\t\t\t\tvar target string\n   380\t\t\t\ttarget, e = os.Readlink(full)\n   381\t\t\t\traw = []byte(target)\n   382\t\t\t} else {\n   383\t\t\t\tif !info.Mode().IsRegular() {\n   384\t\t\t\t\tchanged = append(changed, path)\n   385\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   386\t\t\t\t}\n   387\t\t\t\t// Verify executable materialization even when index flags hide it.\n   388\t\t\t\t// Windows does not materialize POSIX executable bits.\n   389\t\t\t\tif runtime.GOOS != \"windows\" && (info.Mode().Perm()&0111 != 0) != (fields[0] == \"100755\") {\n   390\t\t\t\t\tchanged = append(changed, path)\n   391\t\t\t\t}\n   392\t\t\t\tif info.Size() > budget-total {\n   393\t\t\t\t\treturn nil, &GitSnapshotError{\"read \" + path, fmt.Errorf(\"snapshot exceeds its budget of %d bytes\", budget)}\n   394\t\t\t\t}\n   395\t\t\t\tvar file *os.File\n   396\t\t\t\tfile, e = os.Open(full)\n   397\t\t\t\tif e == nil {\n   398\t\t\t\t\traw, e = io.ReadAll(io.LimitReader(file, budget-total+1))\n   399\t\t\t\t\tcloseErr := file.Close()\n   400\t\t\t\t\tif e == nil {\n   401\t\t\t\t\t\te = closeErr\n   402\t\t\t\t\t}\n   403\t\t\t\t\ttotal += int64(len(raw))\n   404\t\t\t\t\tif total > budget {\n   405\t\t\t\t\t\treturn nil, &GitSnapshotError{\"read \" + path, fmt.Errorf(\"snapshot exceeds its budget of %d bytes\", budget)}\n   406\t\t\t\t\t}\n   407\t\t\t\t}\n   408\t\t\t}\n   409\t\t\tif e != nil {\n   410\t\t\t\treturn nil, &GitSnapshotError{\"read \" + path, e}\n   411\t\t\t}\n   412\t\t\tcmd := gitCommand(\"-C\", root, \"hash-object\", \"--stdin\", \"--path=\"+path)\n   413\t\t\tif fields[0] == \"120000\" {\n   414\t\t\t\tcmd = gitCommand(\"-C\", root, \"hash-object\", \"--stdin\", \"--no-filters\")\n   415\t\t\t}\n   416\t\t\tcmd.Stdin = bytes.NewReader(raw)\n   417\t\t\thash, e := cmd.Output()\n   418\t\t\tif e != nil {\n   419\t\t\t\treturn nil, &GitSnapshotError{\"hash \" + path, e}\n   420\t\t\t}\n   421\t\t\tif strings.TrimSpace(string(hash)) != fields[2] {\n   422\t\t\t\tchanged = append(changed, path)\n   423\t\t\t}\n   424\t\t}\n   425\t\tsort.Strings(changed)\n   426\t\treturn changed, nil\n   427\t}\n   428\t\n   429\t// These readers are shared by the bundle, obligation and execution snapshots.\n   430\tvar ErrGitUnknown = errors.New(\"pose: git state is unknown\")\n   431\tvar ErrGitUnavailable = errors.New(\"pose: not a git repository\")\n   432\t\n   433\tfunc (e *GitSnapshotError) Is(target error) bool { return target == ErrGitUnknown }\n   434\t\n   435\tfunc hasGitMetadata(root string) bool {\n   436\t\tdir, err := filepath.Abs(root)\n   437\t\tif err != nil {\n   438\t\t\treturn true\n   439\t\t}\n   440\t\tif gitMetadataAbove(dir) {\n   441\t\t\treturn true\n   442\t\t}\n   443\t\t// git walks the physical path, and a link can lead out of the lexical one.\n   444\t\tphysical, err := filepath.EvalSymlinks(dir)\n   445\t\treturn err == nil && physical != dir && gitMetadataAbove(physical)\n   446\t}\n   447\t\n   448\tfunc gitMetadataAbove(dir string) bool {\n   449\t\tfor {\n   450\t\t\tif gitMetadataAt(dir) {\n   451\t\t\t\treturn true\n   452\t\t\t}\n   453\t\t\tparent := filepath.Dir(dir)\n   454\t\t\tif parent == dir {\n   455\t\t\t\treturn false\n   456\t\t\t}\n   457\t\t\tdir = parent\n   458\t\t}\n   459\t}\n   460\t\nartifact.spec=pose-git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree\nartifact.change_set=cs-3764e4bde0e1\nartifact.change_set.base=ca66b779b3c83932c3273427ad1cd8c3c7a40a98\nartifact.change_set.head=8432edbf039ff268cb56907f8272c479c503d51a\nartifact.change_set.commits=30\nartifact.diff_digest=sha256:3a19a1b32d81916d1aada6ceec0d0fcbaa2ad1e77ec54a843498c3b908980522\nartifact.claims=8\nartifact.observed=43\nartifact.findings=975\n[!] warning orphan pose-mcp/internal/cli/update_reports_delivered_state_test.go\n    governed tracked path has no spec provenance claim\n    fix: backfill an explicit claim or add an exact reviewed exclusion\n[!] warning orphan pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_routing_test.go\n    governed tracked path has no spec provenance claim\n    fix: backfill an explicit claim or add an exact reviewed exclusion\n[!] warning orphan pose-mcp/internal/cli/state_hooks_test.go\n    governed tracked path has no spec provenance claim\n    fix: backfill an explicit claim or add an exact reviewed exclusion\n[!] warning orphan .github/workflows/security.yml\n    governed tracked path has no spec provenance claim\n    fix: backfill an explicit claim or add an exact reviewed exclusion\n[!] wa