{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: approved\n\nNo new defects found. Both prior blockers are fixed. The sweep covered budget calculation, bounded listings, governed read-view capture and audit, cleanup ownership, regression tests, validation wiring, and all four manuals.\n\nApplied the review workflow and Go, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence rules. Tests were assessed from the sealed results and source; no builds, repository changes, or attestations were made. The surface check passed. For artifact attribution, I used the supplied output matching the sealed head because the rerun resolved a later range head.\n\nReviewed bundle: `rvb-60c8431d4eb8b227`, digest `sha256:60c8431d4eb8b2274844b996601267a386ae085bd909373283ba6c67a4e91c8c`.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R2-N2\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"git_snapshot_integrity.go:50-56 bounds listings before retention; dispatchDiskSnapshot uses it at lines 84-86; review_adapter_containment.go:474-477 uses it for cleanup budgeting. git_snapshot_budget_test.go:159-216 covers comparison, disk snapshot, cleanup fallback, governed byte limits and deadlines.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R3-N4\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"git_snapshot_integrity.go:246-252 uses CaptureGovernanceGitContextIn with the listing-specific byte limit and deadline under a producer. git_snapshot_budget_test.go:186-216 exercises the closeout-plan producer through a real read view. governance_read_view_git.go:337-338,395,525-529 preserves audit provenance and the deadline without retaining caller cancellation.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed requirements R1-R5 and decision D1; all attributed implementation changes, start metadata, validation-matrix changes and four manual updates; production callers in closeout_plan.go and review_dispatch.go; bounded Git capture, read-view admission, memoization and audit; cleanup registration ownership and inventory-before-removal; all new positive and negative regression tests; sealed validation results and supplied artifact/surface outputs. Ran context resolution, suggest review, bundle explain, artifact-check, surface-check, recurrence-check, diff whitespace checks and worktree status checks. No new defects established; worktree remained unchanged.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Verified stored blob sizes determine the budget, rather than materialized sizes. Tests establish clean-tree coverage and refusal of excess growth. R1 explicitly excludes expansion beyond the margin; R3 specifies margin-only disk fallback when listing fails. The 4 GiB ceiling and future retention work remain explicit spec limitations. No unresolved assumption needed for approval.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Both listing routes have a two-minute context and use the synchronized bounded-output runner with bounded pipe waiting. Read-view capture retains its existing locking and admission accounting. Deadline regressions cover governed and ungoverned routes. Test-only limit mutations occur in sequential tests and are restored.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-and-dispatch-snapshot-integrity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"No exported CLI, MCP, event or persisted-file schema changed. The internal ls-tree parser changes consistently with the added size column.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Listing bytes and duration are bounded before retention. Snapshot excess returns a budget-naming error; listing failures prevent comparison, while disk and cleanup budgeting conservatively fall back to the margin. Negative tests exercise each affected route.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Checked the closeout-plan producer path and delegated review setup/snapshot/cleanup callers. Cleanup derives its budget from the coordinator repository and captured detached commit; governed comparison preserves read-view provenance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Snapshot errors include the computed budget and retain GitSnapshotError context. Listing capture uses bounded diagnostics. Cleanup retains its existing operational failure and resource-retention reporting without exposing captured content.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-and-dispatch-snapshot-integrity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined public interfaces, persisted cleanup observations and internal parser consumers. Public contracts remain unchanged; the content allowance grows from the existing margin, subject to the explicitly required metadata and absolute ceilings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed budget floor/ceiling arithmetic, committed-size parsing, cumulative read limits, cleanup preflight and regression assertions. Tests cover trees larger than the margin, excess materialized growth, listing overflow, deadlines and cleanup retention.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-f8fb0b4b635b0d5b\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D1 addresses the actual cause: a fixed content allowance below the committed tree made complete comparison impossible. The shared tree-plus-margin calculation follows required work while retaining a ceiling. The permanent integration check binds R1-R5 to executable regression coverage.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-83889a63\",\n          \"basis\": \"R1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The validation-matrix addition registers the required git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree integration command that exercises R1 and the related R2-R5 budget and containment requirements.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Checked the English and Portuguese root and scaffold manual changes. All describe the committed-tree-plus-256 MiB workspace allowance, 256 MiB floor and 4 GiB ceiling, while preserving entry, registration, runtime and filesystem-latency qualifications.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined budget errors, conservative fallback and cleanup refusal. Oversized snapshots identify their allowance; failed cleanup retains resources and continues to block authority. Existing safety documentation explains inspection and recovery without respawning the adapter.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R1 is covered by committed-tree snapshot/comparison tests; R2 by growth refusal; R3 by floor/ceiling and failed-listing fallback assertions; R4 by real registered-worktree cleanup and retention tests; R5 by byte and deadline tests including the governed producer route.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-f8fb0b4b635b0d5b\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared the attributed subject with the spec artifacts and production composition. Changes remain confined to snapshot and cleanup budgeting, regression coverage, validation wiring and corresponding manuals. Retention policy and the 100000-entry limit remain outside this implementation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-adapter-containment-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed bounded capture and cleanup authority. Listing output is admitted before retention; cleanup reads commit metadata from the coordinator, preserves descriptor confinement and ownership checks, and inventories before deletion. No secret material or new execution authority is introduced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-f8fb0b4b635b0d5b\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared D1 with raising the fixed constant and introducing retention. One shared budget helper and reuse of the existing bounded Git runner are sufficient for the stated defect without new public configuration or storage machinery. The choice needs reconsideration when tree size reaches the absolute ceiling or retention cost dominates, as the spec records.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran successfully, but the rerun resolved a later range head. For this sealed subject, inspected /var/tmp/closeout/ac-bg.out, which identifies cs-3764e4bde0e1 and head 8432edbf039ff268cb56907f8272c479c503d51a. Its findings are repository-wide orphan warnings; no scoped attribution error was established.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-f8fb0b4b635b0d5b\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Assessment reruns write repository state and were prohibited. Independently inspected D1, R1-R5, the structural delta and implementation; used the sealed design evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose context --task spec:pose-git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree --json\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Discovery writes assessment state and was prohibited. Context resolution confirmed the authority and sealed revision; component scope was inspected directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Assessment writes were prohibited. Inspected production callers and read-view capture boundaries directly and evaluated sealed integration evidence; no public inter-module contract changed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:rg -n 'TODO|FIXME|stub|panic' pose-mcp/internal/po